# Documentation system

## Goal

Write docs so a coding assistant reads the fewest tokens. Open only the files required for the current task.

## Locations and names

- Concept or reusable term: `docs/concepts/c-<slug>.md`
- Plan: `docs/plans/p-<slug>.md`
- Prompt: `docs/prompts/<slug>/YYYY-MM-DD-HHmm-<action>-<slug>-phase-<n>.md`
- Map: `docs/README.md`

`<slug>` is kebab-case. Prompt folder uses the feature slug with no `c-` or `p-` prefix.

Example: concept `docs/concepts/c-player-inventory.md`, plan `docs/plans/p-player-inventory.md`, prompt `docs/prompts/player-inventory/2026-09-27-1204-add-player-inventory-phase-1.md`

## One definition

Each idea or term is defined in exactly one file. Other files link to it. Never copy or restate a definition.

Link form: `[Player inventory](../concepts/c-player-inventory.md)`

## Index

`docs/README.md` is links only: title + path. No summaries. Adding a new link there does not need permission. Changing definition text does.

## Permission

Do not edit an existing concept, plan, prompt, or this rule unless the developer gives explicit permission in the same conversation. New files are allowed.

## Conflicts

Before adding a file, open the related existing docs via their links. If anything conflicts, stop and ask. Do not silently rewrite the old doc.

## Concept

One file. Holistic. Defines the idea, high-level feature or vision, and the value it adds to the system. Not an implementation spec.

## Plan

How to add one or more features to the current project.

- Functional and non-functional requirements (link to concepts; do not redefine them)
- One or more phases
- Each phase has one or more implementation prompts

## Prompt

Implementation instructions for one plan phase. The assistant must not guess.

- Filename and the first lines include the timestamp `YYYY-MM-DD-HHmm`
- Link the plan and every concept the work depends on
- Super detailed: files, behavior, acceptance, out of scope

### Before writing a prompt

1. List every vague point.
2. For each point, recommend an option and give alternatives.
3. Wait for the developer to decide.
4. Write the prompt from those decisions.

Design decisions belong to the developer. Recommendations are advisory.

## Read path

Need a term → open that one concept file. Implementing a phase → open that prompt + only the concepts it links. Do not load the whole `docs/` tree.
